  {
    "id": "what",
    "title": "A constitution open to correction",
    "labels": [
      "Cosmolocalism",
      "Ownership and voice",
      "Ten clauses"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "It proposes constitutional cosmolocalism: global knowledge, distributed capacities, and rights beyond local goodwill.",
      "Artificial intelligence and basic income are tested by who owns, who controls, and who speaks.",
      "Its light is modest: institutions where errors become information and leaders can be replaced peacefully.",
      "Start with the introduction, When the Exit Resembles the Entrance, then test the ten clauses yourself."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "constructive proposal to a personal, open invitation",
      "purpose": "Present the proposal and its test, then give a concrete starting point.",
      "states": [
        "constructive confidence",
        "probing realism",
        "conviction",
        "inviting openness"
      ],
      "intensities": [
        0.5,
        0.55,
        0.7,
        0.45
      ],
      "voiceDirections": [
        "Clear and deliberate; enunciate 'cosmolocalism' without rushing.",
        "Even, questioning tone; stress the three tests lightly.",
        "Slow, earnest, close to the listener; let 'modest' sound like strength.",
        "Warm and direct, like handing over the book."
      ]
    },
